"kopiaste.org","note":"Long-running blog of Greek and Cypriot home recipes.","url":"https://www.kopiaste.org/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"Dimitra's Dishes","ref":"site/dimitrasdishes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dimitrasdishes.com","note":"Dimitra Alfieris's video channel and blog focused on classic Greek home cooking.","url":"https://dimitrasdishes.com","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Cypriot cuisine","links":[["Mujaddara","dish/mujaddara"],["Stuffed squash","dish/stuffed-squash"]]}]},"ingredient/meatball":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/meatball","n":"Meatball","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 4 dishes across 5 cuisines","intro":[["A meatball is ground meat (mince) rolled into a large somewhat spherical ball, sometimes along with other ingredients, such as bread crumbs, minced onion, eggs, butter, and seasoning. Meatballs are cooked by frying, baking, steaming, or braising in sauce. There are many types of meatballs made with different meats and spices. The term is sometimes extended to meatless versions based on legumes, vegetables, mushrooms, fish (also commonly known as fish balls) or other seafood."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-meatball"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meatball"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":5,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Meatball sandwich","dish/meatball-sandwich"]]],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Mie kocok","dish/mie-kocok"]]],["Italian-American cuisine","cuisine/italian-american-cuisine",[["Spaghetti and meatballs","dish/spaghetti-and-meatballs"]]],["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Gondi (food)","dish/gondi-food"]]],["Mizrahi Jewish cuisine","cuisine/mizrahi-jewish-cuisine",[["Gondi (food)","dish/gondi-food"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Besan","ingredient/besan"],["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Chicken","ingredi